<title>UK: Internet seen boosting UK phone usage -- paper.</title>
<headline>Internet seen boosting UK phone usage -- paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Personal computers connected to the Internet account for much of the recent jump in British phone usage, according to a report in the Financial Times.</p>
<p>The paper said Internet use accounted for about 10 percent of local call traffic and was behind the rise in growth in volume to seven percent in 1996 from five percent the year before.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
